# Probate and Administration Act 1934

## 0. What this Act adds to the shared ontology

<!-- l4: declare:Applicant -->

**1.** In this Act, “Applicant” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “name”, being a STRING;

    (b) “has renounced the right to such grant”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “the Public Trustee”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “a corporation licensed as a trust company under the Trust Companies Act 2005”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “an infant”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “lacks mental capacity”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (g) “an executor appointed by the will”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (h) “legally incapable of acting as such”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (i) “survives the testator”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (j) “died before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (k) “appears and extracts probate”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (l) “a universal or residuary legatee”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (m) “a legal personal representative of a deceased universal or residuary legatee”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (n) “a beneficiary under the will who would have been entitled to a grant of letters of administration if the deceased had died intestate”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (o) “a legatee having a beneficial interest”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (p) “a creditor of the deceased”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (q) “the husband or widow or next of kin”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (r) “an applicant for the grant”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: declare:Administration -->

**2.** In this Act, “Administration” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “case”, being a Case;

    (b) “persons who are or may become entitled to probate or letters of administration”, being a list of Applicant;

    (c) “the date as at which the question is asked”, being a DATE;

    (d) “there is a minority or a life interest arises under the will”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “a probate action is pending”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “a general caveat has been entered”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (g) “the caveator has been given opportunity to contest”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (h) “an application has been made for probate or letters of administration”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (i) “the application has been proceeded with, and has not been withdrawn or refused”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (j) “the administrator has extracted the grant of letters of administration”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (k) “date of the grant”, being an optional DATE;

    (l) “granted by a Family Court”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (m) “the person for whose use and benefit the grant is made is an infant”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (n) “the Family Court thinks fit to require such security”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (o) “the administrator is entitled to the whole of the estate after payment of the debts”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (p) “the amount at which the estate within the jurisdiction is sworn”, being a NUMBER;

    (q) “debts due by the deceased secured by mortgage”, being a NUMBER;

    (r) “such security as he is lawfully required to furnish has been given”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (s) “date of death of the last surviving executor or administrator”, being an optional DATE;

    (t) “an application for the representation of the estate has been made since that death”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (u) “there is danger that the property may be wasted”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (v) “the appointment of a receiver would be a sufficient protection for the estate”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (w) “the Public Trustee has declared that he undertakes to administer the property”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (x) “the value of the assets collected by them”, being a NUMBER; and

    (y) “the order of application is varied by the will of the deceased”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: declare:Kind of grant -->

**3.** In this Act, “Kind of grant” means one of the following—

    (a) “probate”;

    (b) “letters of administration with the will annexed”;

    (c) “letters of administration”;

    (d) “letters of administration pending probate action”; or

    (e) “no grant”.

<!-- l4: declare:Grant of representation -->

**4.** In this Act, “Grant of representation” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “kind”, being a Kind of grant;

    (b) “name”, being a STRING; and

    (c) “basis”, being a STRING.

<!-- l4: declare:Rule of application -->

**5.** In this Act, “Rule of application” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “paragraph”, being a NUMBER; and

    (b) “text”, being a STRING.

<!-- l4: declare:Application of assets -->

**6.** In this Act, “Application of assets” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “solvent”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (b) “schedule”, being a STRING;

    (c) “rules”, being a list of Rule of application; and

    (d) “basis”, being a STRING.

<!-- l4: declare:Timeline event -->

**7.** In this Act, “Timeline event” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “date”, being a DATE;

    (b) “event”, being a STRING; and

    (c) “basis”, being a STRING.

<!-- l4: declare:Charged interest -->

**8.** In this Act, “Charged interest” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “description”, being a STRING;

    (b) “value”, being a NUMBER;

    (c) “charged with the payment of money at the time of his death”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “a contrary or other intention signified by will, deed or other document”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (e) “that intention signified only by a general direction for the payment of debts or by a charge of debts upon the residuary estate”, being a BOOLEAN.

## Part 1 — Preliminary

<!-- l4: decide:the section 2 definition of -->

**9.** In relation to a Kind of grant “k”, the section 2 definition of means consider the case distinctions of k :  when probate has  then a grant under the seal of the court issuing the same, authorising the executor or executors expressly or impliedly appointed by a testator's will, or one or more of them, to administer the testator's estate in compliance with the directions contained in his will, and in accordance with law. when letters of administration with the will annexed has  then a grant under the seal of the court issuing the same, authorising the person or persons therein named to administer a testator's estate in compliance with the directions contained in his will, and in accordance with law. when letters of administration has  then a grant under the seal of the court issuing the same, authorising the person or persons therein named to administer an intestate's estate in accordance with law. when letters of administration pending probate action has  then letters of administration granted pending a probate action under section 20, limited so that the administrator shall not be empowered to distribute the estate. when no grant has  then no grant of representation: under section 62 the Public Trustee may declare that he undertakes to administer property in Singapore not exceeding $50,000 in value.

<!-- l4: decide:the deceased left a will in -->

**10.** In relation to an Administration “a”, the deceased left a will in means consider the case distinctions of a's case's will :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has w then TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the deceased died intestate in -->

**11.** In relation to an Administration “a”, the deceased died intestate in if it is not the case that the deceased left a will in with a.

## Part 2 — Renunciation

<!-- l4: decide:renunciation precludes -->

**12.** In relation to an Applicant “p”, renunciation precludes means p's has renounced the right to such grant.

## Part 3 — Grant of probate or letters of administration

<!-- l4: decide:a trust corporation for the purposes of section 6 is -->

**13.** In relation to an Applicant “p”, a trust corporation for the purposes of section 6 is if—

    (a) p's the Public Trustee; or

    (b) p's a corporation licensed as a trust company under the Trust Companies Act 2005.

<!-- l4: decide:the applicants for a grant in -->

**14.** In relation to an Administration “a”, the applicants for a grant in means filter with given p then p's an applicant for the grant and a grant may be made to with p and everyone.

For the purposes of this provision—

“everyone” means a's persons who are or may become entitled to probate or letters of administration;

<!-- l4: decide:the grant complies with section 6(1) in -->

**15.** In relation to an Administration “a”, the grant complies with section 6(1) in means count with applicants is at most 4.

For the purposes of this provision—

“applicants” means the applicants for a grant in with a;

<!-- l4: decide:the grant complies with section 6(2) in -->

**16.** In relation to an Administration “a”, the grant complies with section 6(2) in means if not the grant is an administration in with a then TRUE if not a's there is a minority or a life interest arises under the will then TRUE otherwise any with given p then a trust corporation for the purposes of section 6 is with p and applicants or count with individuals is at least 2 where  and.

<!-- l4: decide:section 21(1) refuses a grant to -->

**17.** In relation to an Applicant “p”, section 21(1) refuses a grant to means p's an infant.

<!-- l4: decide:section 22(1) refuses a grant to -->

**18.** In relation to an Applicant “p”, section 22(1) refuses a grant to means p's lacks mental capacity.

<!-- l4: decide:a grant may be made to -->

**19.** In relation to an Applicant “p”, a grant may be made to if—

    (a) it is not the case that renunciation precludes with p;

    (b) it is not the case that section 21(1) refuses a grant to with p; and

    (c) it is not the case that section 22(1) refuses a grant to with p.

<!-- l4: decide:probate may be granted to -->

**20.** In relation to an Applicant “p”, probate may be granted to if—

    (a) p's an executor appointed by the will;

    (b) p's survives the testator;

    (c) it is not the case that p's legally incapable of acting as such;

    (d) it is not the case that p's died before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased; and

    (e) a grant may be made to with p.

<!-- l4: decide:the executors appointed by the will in -->

**21.** In relation to an Administration “a”, the executors appointed by the will in means filter with given p then p's an executor appointed by the will and everyone.

For the purposes of this provision—

“everyone” means a's persons who are or may become entitled to probate or letters of administration;

<!-- l4: decide:the executors to whom probate may be granted in -->

**22.** In relation to an Administration “a”, the executors to whom probate may be granted in means filter with given p then probate may be granted to with p and everyone.

For the purposes of this provision—

“everyone” means a's persons who are or may become entitled to probate or letters of administration;

<!-- l4: decide:section 13(1)(a) no executor is appointed by a will in -->

**23.** In relation to an Administration “a”, section 13(1)(a) no executor is appointed by a will in means count with executors is equal to 0.

For the purposes of this provision—

“executors” means the executors appointed by the will in with a;

<!-- l4: decide:section 13(1)(b) the executors are legally incapable or have renounced in -->

**24.** In relation to an Administration “a”, section 13(1)(b) the executors are legally incapable or have renounced in means all with given p then p's legally incapable of acting as such or p's has renounced the right to such grant and executors.

For the purposes of this provision—

“executors” means the executors appointed by the will in with a;

<!-- l4: decide:section 13(1)(c) no executor survives the testator in -->

**25.** In relation to an Administration “a”, section 13(1)(c) no executor survives the testator in means all with given p then not p's survives the testator and executors.

For the purposes of this provision—

“executors” means the executors appointed by the will in with a;

<!-- l4: decide:section 13(1)(d) all the executors die before obtaining probate in -->

**26.** In relation to an Administration “a”, section 13(1)(d) all the executors die before obtaining probate in means all with given p then p's died before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased and executors.

For the purposes of this provision—

“executors” means the executors appointed by the will in with a;

<!-- l4: decide:section 13(1)(e) the executors do not appear and extract probate in -->

**27.** In relation to an Administration “a”, section 13(1)(e) the executors do not appear and extract probate in means all with given p then not p's appears and extracts probate and executors.

For the purposes of this provision—

“executors” means the executors appointed by the will in with a;

<!-- l4: decide:there is a failure of executors in -->

**28.** In relation to an Administration “a”, there is a failure of executors in if—

    (a) section 13(1)(a) no executor is appointed by a will in with a;

    (b) section 13(1)(b) the executors are legally incapable or have renounced in with a;

    (c) section 13(1)(c) no executor survives the testator in with a;

    (d) section 13(1)(d) all the executors die before obtaining probate in with a; or

    (e) section 13(1)(e) the executors do not appear and extract probate in with a.

<!-- l4: decide:the section 13(2) rank of -->

**29.** In relation to an Applicant “p”, the section 13(2) rank of means if p's a universal or residuary legatee then 1 if p's a legal personal representative of a deceased universal or residuary legatee then 2 if p's a beneficiary under the will who would have been entitled to a grant of letters of administration if the deceased had died intestate then 3 if p's a legatee having a beneficial interest then 4 if p's a creditor of the deceased then 5 otherwise 6.

<!-- l4: decide:those with a prior right under section 13(2) in -->

**30.** In relation to an Administration “a”, those with a prior right under section 13(2) in means filter with given p then the section 13(2) rank of with p is equal to best and candidates.

For the purposes of this provision—

“everyone” means a's persons who are or may become entitled to probate or letters of administration;

“candidates” means filter with given p then a grant may be made to with p and everyone;

“ranks” means map with given p then the section 13(2) rank of with p and candidates;

“best” means minimum1 with 6 and ranks;

<!-- l4: decide:letters of administration may be granted on intestacy in -->

**31.** In relation to an Administration “a”, letters of administration may be granted on intestacy in means the deceased died intestate in with a.

<!-- l4: decide:a person in the section 18(4)(a) class has applied in -->

**32.** In relation to an Administration “a”, a person in the section 18(4)(a) class has applied in means any with given p then p's the husband or widow or next of kin and p's an applicant for the grant and candidates.

For the purposes of this provision—

“everyone” means a's persons who are or may become entitled to probate or letters of administration;

“candidates” means filter with given p then a grant may be made to with p and everyone;

<!-- l4: decide:the section 18(4) rank in -->

**33.** In relation to an Administration “a” and an Applicant “p”, the section 18(4) rank in means if p's the husband or widow or next of kin and p's an applicant for the grant then 1 if p's a creditor of the deceased and p's an applicant for the grant and not a person in the section 18(4)(a) class has applied in with a then 2 otherwise 3.

<!-- l4: decide:those who may be granted letters of administration under section 18(4) in -->

**34.** In relation to an Administration “a”, those who may be granted letters of administration under section 18(4) in means filter with given p then the section 18(4) rank in _ of _ with a and p is equal to best and candidates.

For the purposes of this provision—

“everyone” means a's persons who are or may become entitled to probate or letters of administration;

“candidates” means filter with given p then a grant may be made to with p and everyone;

“ranks” means map with given p then the section 18(4) rank in _ of _ with a and p and candidates;

“best” means minimum1 with 3 and ranks;

<!-- l4: decide:letters of administration pending probate action may be granted in -->

**35.** In relation to an Administration “a”, letters of administration pending probate action may be granted in means a's a probate action is pending.

<!-- l4: decide:a further grant may be made on the death of an administrator in -->

**36.** In relation to an Administration “a”, a further grant may be made on the death of an administrator in means consider the case distinctions of a's date of death of the last surviving executor or administrator :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has d then TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the section 62 threshold -->

**37.** The section 62 threshold means 50000.

<!-- l4: decide:the Public Trustee may undertake to administer the property in -->

**38.** In relation to an Administration “a”, the Public Trustee may undertake to administer the property in if—

    (a) gross estate of with c is at most the section 62 threshold; and

    (b) a's an application does not have been made for probate or letters of administration.

For the purposes of this provision—

“c” means a's case;

<!-- l4: decide:the grant of representation in -->

**39.** In relation to an Administration “a”, the grant of representation in means if a's the Public Trustee has declared that he undertakes to administer the property and the Public Trustee may undertake to administer the property in with a then Grant of representation where kind is no grant, name is no grant of representation is required and basis is PAA s 62(1): the deceased left property in Singapore not exceeding $50,000 in value (without deduction for debts), no application for letters of administration is pending, and the Public Trustee has declared that he undertakes to administer it. if letters of administration pending probate action may be granted in with a then Grant of representation where kind is letters of administration pending probate action, name is letters of administration pending probate action and basis is PAA s 20: pending any probate action, letters of administration may be granted to such person as the court may appoint, limited so that the administrator shall not be empowered to distribute the estate. if the deceased left a will in with a and not there is a failure of executors in with a then Grant of representation where kind is probate, name is probate and basis is PAA s 8(1): probate may be granted to any executor appointed by a will. if the deceased left a will in with a then Grant of representation where kind is letters of administration with the will annexed, name is letters of administration with the will annexed and basis is PAA s 13(1): on failure of executors, letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to such person or persons as the court considers the fittest to administer the estate. PAA s 13(2) gives a prior right in order to a universal or residuary legatee, then to a legal personal representative of a deceased universal or residuary legatee, then to beneficiaries who would have been entitled on intestacy, then to a legatee having a beneficial interest, then to a creditor. otherwise Grant of representation where kind is letters of administration, name is letters of administration and basis is PAA s 18(1): when a person has died intestate, the court may grant letters of administration of his estate. PAA s 18(4) names the husband or widow or next of kin, or if none applies a creditor, or such person as the court thinks fit..

<!-- l4: decide:the grant is an administration in -->

**40.** In relation to an Administration “a”, the grant is an administration in means consider the case distinctions of g's kind :  when probate has  then FALSE. when letters of administration with the will annexed has  then TRUE. when letters of administration has  then TRUE. when letters of administration pending probate action has  then TRUE. when no grant has  then FALSE.

For the purposes of this provision—

“g” means the grant of representation in with a;

<!-- l4: decide:the name of the grant in -->

**41.** In relation to an Administration “a”, the name of the grant in means g's name.

For the purposes of this provision—

“g” means the grant of representation in with a;

<!-- l4: decide:those who may take the grant in -->

**42.** In relation to an Administration “a”, those who may take the grant in means consider the case distinctions of g's kind :  when probate has  then the executors to whom probate may be granted in with a. when letters of administration with the will annexed has  then those with a prior right under section 13(2) in with a. when letters of administration has  then those who may be granted letters of administration under section 18(4) in with a. when letters of administration pending probate action has  then EMPTY. when no grant has  then EMPTY.

For the purposes of this provision—

“g” means the grant of representation in with a;

## Part 4 — Oath

<!-- l4: decide:an oath is required of -->

**43.** In relation to an Applicant “p”, an oath is required of if—

    (a) it is not the case that p's the Public Trustee; and

    (b) it is not the case that p's a corporation licensed as a trust company under the Trust Companies Act 2005.

## Part 5 — Security

<!-- l4: decide:the Public Trustee has obtained the grant in -->

**44.** In relation to an Administration “a”, the Public Trustee has obtained the grant in means any with given p then p's the Public Trustee and applicants.

For the purposes of this provision—

“applicants” means the applicants for a grant in with a;

<!-- l4: decide:security for the due administration of the estate is required in -->

**45.** In relation to an Administration “a”, security for the due administration of the estate is required in means if not the grant is an administration in with a then FALSE if the Public Trustee has obtained the grant in with a then FALSE if a's granted by a Family Court then a's the person for whose use and benefit the grant is made is an infant or a's the Family Court thinks fit to require such security otherwise TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the number of sureties a bond ordinarily requires -->

**46.** The number of sureties a bond ordinarily requires means 2.

<!-- l4: decide:the number of sureties required in -->

**47.** In relation to an Administration “a”, the number of sureties required in means if not security for the due administration of the estate is required in with a then 0 if a's the administrator is entitled to the whole of the estate after payment of the debts then 0 otherwise the number of sureties a bond ordinarily requires.

<!-- l4: decide:the amount of the bond in -->

**48.** In relation to an Administration “a”, the amount of the bond in means if not security for the due administration of the estate is required in with a, then 0; otherwise, the difference between mortgages and sworn.

For the purposes of this provision—

“sworn” means a's the amount at which the estate within the jurisdiction is sworn;

“mortgages” means a's debts due by the deceased secured by mortgage;

<!-- l4: decide:a bond under section 30 may be required in -->

**49.** In relation to an Administration “a”, a bond under section 30 may be required in if—

    (a) the grant is an administration in with a; and

    (b) any with given p then p's a creditor of the deceased and applicants.

For the purposes of this provision—

