## Part 7 — Caveats

<!-- l4: decide:a caveat bars the grant in -->

**50.** In relation to an Administration “a”, a caveat bars the grant in if—

    (a) a's a general caveat has been entered; and

    (b) a's the caveator does not have been given opportunity to contest.

## Part 9 — Protection of estates pending grant

<!-- l4: decide:a grant has been made in -->

**51.** In relation to an Administration “a”, a grant has been made in means consider the case distinctions of a's date of the grant :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has d then TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:there is no executor with power to obtain probate in -->

**52.** In relation to an Administration “a”, there is no executor with power to obtain probate in if—

    (a) the deceased died intestate in with a; or

    (b) all of the following apply—

        (i) the deceased left a will in with a; and

        (ii) there is a failure of executors in with a.

<!-- l4: decide:the estate vests in the Public Trustee under section 37 in -->

**53.** In relation to an Administration “a”, the estate vests in the Public Trustee under section 37 in if—

    (a) there is no executor with power to obtain probate in with a; and

    (b) a grant does not have been made in with a.

<!-- l4: decide:a receiver may be appointed under section 39 in -->

**54.** In relation to an Administration “a”, a receiver may be appointed under section 39 in if—

    (a) a's there is danger that the property may be wasted; and

    (b) a grant does not have been made in with a.

